					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-442977#post-1500659</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-442977/scp-4357-j#post-1500659</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 06 Jul 2012 20:10:33 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TheGlyphstone</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1359260</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I think it's because they have a higher expected standard. Almost anyone can write horror, or at least creepy, but it's much harder to write comedy. Plus, the much smaller number of -J's compared to regular articles means a mediocre or bad addition will stand out more; even if it survives its inception, it's at higher risk of eventual deletion.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
